<article class="env-lemma" id="02UQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02UQ">Lemma <span data-tag="02UQ">10.137.18</span>.</a> Let $K/k$ be a field extension. Let $S$ be a finite type algebra over $k$. Let $\mathfrak q_ K$ be a prime of $S_ K = K \otimes _ k S$ and let $\mathfrak q$ be the corresponding prime of $S$. Then $S$ is smooth over $k$ at $\mathfrak q$ if and only if $S_ K$ is smooth at $\mathfrak q_ K$ over $K$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/00TG" data-tag="00TG">10.137.17</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>